  "definition": "Storage Above Liquid Level; Septic Tank Dimensions",
  "effectiveDate": "2026-02-01",
  "expirationDate": "2036-02-01",
  "historyNote": "(See Revision Notes #1 and #2 at chapter heading for Env-Wq 1000) #11184, eff 10-1-16; ss by #14486, eff 2-1-26, EXPIRES: 2-1-36",
  "inScheme": "https://granitestate.github.io/rules/scheme",
  "notation": "Env-Wq 1010.09",
  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-wq1000.html",
  "prefLabel": "Env-Wq 1010.09 Storage Above Liquid Level; Septic Tank Dimensions",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wq 1010.09 Storage Above Liquid Level; Septic Tank Dimensions.\n\n(a) The distance between the liquid line and the interior surface of the top of the tank shall be equal to approximately 20% of the liquid depth.\n\n(b) The interior of the septic tank shall provide:\n\n(1) A total liquid surface area of not less than 25 SF; and\n\n(2) A total length of not less than 6 feet between the inlet and the outlet of the septic tank.\n\nSource. (See Revision Notes #1 and #2 at chapter heading for Env-Wq 1000) #11184, eff 10-1-16; ss by #14486, eff 2-1-26, EXPIRES: 2-1-36",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-wq1000.html"
